<summary>Reproduction driver and commands</summary>

Save the driver below as `proof.mjs` outside the source checkout. Use the exact pinned upstream source for baseline and exact candidate tree for candidate, each with its own normal frozen-lockfile dependencies and isolated output. Our executions reused one checkout sequentially, preserving/restoring candidate bytes; there was no owner-file overlay, new worktree, timer shortening or injected watchdog outcome.

```sh
# From the qualified source checkout; Node24.22.1 and repository-pinned pnpm12.15.
export QA_WATCHDOG_PROOF_REPO="$PWD"
export QA_WATCHDOG_PROOF_BASE=d3b77ae4921503f12676881f065be539d755887d
export QA_WATCHDOG_PROOF_ARM=candidate # baseline for the complete pinned upstream
export QA_WATCHDOG_PROOF_ROUTES=all # announce for the affected-path follow-up
export QA_WATCHDOG_PROOF_OUT="$(mktemp -d)"
export QA_EXPECTED_SOURCE_DIFF_SHA256="$(git diff --binary "$QA_WATCHDOG_PROOF_BASE" | shasum -a 256 | cut -d ' ' -f 1)"
node scripts/prepare-vitest-runtime.mjs --with-ai-package
QA_WATCHDOG_PREFLIGHT_ONLY=1 node --import ./scripts/tsx.mjs /path/to/proof.mjs
QA_WATCHDOG_PREFLIGHT_ONLY=0 node --import ./scripts/tsx.mjs /path/to/proof.mjs
