## What Problem This Solves

During Git-based updates, users cannot see download percentage, received bytes, or speed while a fetch is running.

## User Impact

User impact: source-update users get Git's numeric transfer feedback in the active terminal step, or at most one transfer update every five seconds when output is redirected. `--json` remains a single JSON result without transfer text.

The installed updater must contain this feature before it can display progress. Retry policy and persistent state are unchanged. The maintainer product decision requested in the first ClawSweeper review remains for maintainers before merge.

## Why This Change Was Made

Forward bounded, numeric Git stderr progress through the existing command runner and presenter. Display failures warn once and let the download continue. The existing owners retain retries, cancellation, deadlines, admission and durable history.

The review repair keeps the actual Git error first in saved failure summaries while retaining the complete stderr for existing cause extraction. Ref-lock failures therefore remain actionable, including when SSH authentication details precede Git's fatal summary. Raw stderr capture is unchanged.

